WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:03.389
Yippee ki-yay movie lovers, it's Jan here!

00:00:03.389 --> 00:00:07.320
Like many fans, I thought Gal Gadot's Wonder
Woman really kicked ass on the big screen

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.690
in Batman v Superman.

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:13.919
And with this year marking the 75th anniversary
of the first appearance of Wonder Woman aka

00:00:13.919 --> 00:00:19.090
Diana Prince in All Star Comics No. 8, and
with her first live-action solo movie coming

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:23.939
out next year, I wanted to take a look at
5 cool facts you need to know about Gal Gadot's

00:00:23.939 --> 00:00:26.560
Wonder Woman!

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.320
When creating Wonder Woman's new costume,
the designers wanted to ensure it reflected

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:33.170
the fact she's been around for thousands of
years.

00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:37.530
Costume designer Michael Wilkinson drew on
gladiator and warrior influences for the breastplate,

00:00:37.530 --> 00:00:38.969
split skirt and armor.

00:00:38.969 --> 00:00:43.390
Initially, Zack Snyder wanted her costume
to be made from metal, however this was impractical

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:47.950
as Wonder Woman's stunt sequences and choreography
require her to be able to move with ease.

00:00:47.950 --> 00:00:51.789
In the end, the costume designers developed
a material that looked metallic but still

00:00:51.789 --> 00:00:55.879
allowed for flexibility of movement, and the
breastplate was designed with expansion joints

00:00:55.879 --> 00:00:59.570
that allow Gal Gadot to breathe and perform
her stunt moves more easily.

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:03.989
To finish the costume, it was given a distressed
feel with sword cuts and nicks to show "centuries

00:01:03.989 --> 00:01:06.480
of wear from battle".

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:10.520
Wonder Woman's eagle motif appears throughout
her costume, weapons and new logo.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:14.000
You can see the eagle in her breastplate,
but you might not have spotted the eagle symbol

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.180
engraved into the upper part of her sword.

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:20.280
There's also an eagle emblem in the centre
of her shield, although in Batman V Superman

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:24.340
it's hardly visible as the shield is very
old and the eagle emblem has been worn down

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:27.450
from use in battle.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:31.740
Just like Superman's hidden Kryptonian quote
in his suit, Wonder Woman's sword and shield

00:01:31.740 --> 00:01:35.180
also contain an encrypted quote by American
author Joseph Campbell.

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:39.620
The quote was translated by a linguist into
a "hybrid extinct language" and is engraved

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:42.250
into the sword's blade and around the rim
of the shield.

00:01:42.250 --> 00:01:45.869
The quote is from Campbell's book "Goddesses:
Mystery of the Feminine Divine" and reads

00:01:45.869 --> 00:01:49.990
"Life is killing life all the time and so
the goddess kills herself in the sacrifice

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:51.009
of her own animal."

00:01:51.009 --> 00:01:57.450
For Wonder Woman's iconic lasso, the designers
used a distressed 20-ft gold braid.

00:01:57.450 --> 00:02:02.030
Her belt has a quick-release attachment so
she can access the lasso and it also contains

00:02:02.030 --> 00:02:06.479
a fibre optic cable which lights up and serves
as a reference for the VFX team to enhance

00:02:06.479 --> 00:02:07.909
the lasso's look.

00:02:07.909 --> 00:02:11.540
In previous incarnations of Wonder Woman,
this particular weapon is often called the

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:15.550
Lasso of Truth and anyone caught in it can
be forced to speak truthfully.

00:02:15.550 --> 00:02:19.550
Although, we didn't see this capability in
Batman V Superman, but Zack Snyder has confirmed

00:02:19.550 --> 00:02:22.280
that the lasso "can do that".

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:27.550
Although Gal Gadot already had some combat
training having served in the Israeli army,

00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:31.890
she still had to undertake a demanding training
program to transform herself into the iconic

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:32.890
superheroine.

00:02:32.890 --> 00:02:36.750
She worked with fitness trainer Mark Twight
for over 7 months and trained in sword and

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:41.310
shield play, as well as a range of marital
arts such as kung fu, kickboxing, capoeira

00:02:41.310 --> 00:02:42.420
and jiu jitsu.

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:45.590
According to Gadot as she progressed through
the training she noticed how she "started

00:02:45.590 --> 00:02:50.310
to stand […] and sit differently" and how
satisfying it was to "transform into something

00:02:50.310 --> 00:02:51.310
new."

